  "use_rules": [
    "Public price verification does not establish intended-use permission, selected account/model entitlement, capacity, quality, or owner approval.",
    "All eligible_for_feasibility flags are false while the linked conditions are unresolved; no GO or pack-sale claim follows from this file.",
    "Unknown required costs are null with TODO-VERIFY. Never coerce null to zero, drop an unknown component, or silently use a source observation as an approved operational rate.",
    "Select a model ID, provider, tier, endpoint, billing mode and valid price period together. effective_from/effective_until are inclusive dates; null means the source did not publish that boundary.",
    "Refresh public rates and reconcile contracted prices before financial decisions, registry enablement and Phase 6; fail closed on stale or changed evidence.",
    "Prices cover uncached online text inference only. Treat optional tools, cache storage, batch/flex, non-text modalities, taxes, FX and platform charges separately; no optional-cost route may run with unknown rates.",
    "Use authoritative billable usage, including billed reasoning and retry/fallback attempts, rather than visible output length. Confirm model-specific token/neuron billing and rounding before caps.",
    "Cloudflare displayed token equivalents are rounded. For a conservative scenario use the greater of displayed token cost or neuron-meter cost, then verify invoice rounding and other charges. Do not add both representations. The daily included allocation is shared across models.",
    "OpenRouter credit-purchase fees are acquisition costs, not a surcharge per inference request. Allocate once from actual credit purchases and verify gross/net basis and minimum fee.",
    "Choose a customer collection route: SSLCommerz aggregation or a direct MFS contract. Do not add direct bKash/Nagad fees on top of aggregator channel fees without evidence of a separate contracted charge.",
    "The hypothetical SRS 9.4 rates remain demonstration fixtures and are not imported here as current market prices."
  ],
